{
  "info": {
    "name": "Setor.in API",
    "description": "Setor.in backend collection — happy path only.\n\n## Auto-token magic\nThis collection has a **collection-level pre-request script** that auto-fetches a fresh token before EVERY request when the saved one is missing or expired. You don't need to manually run Login first — just hit any request and the script handles it.\n\nFolder `01 — Auth (Keycloak)` is kept for explicit login/refresh, but you'll rarely need it.\n\n## Setup\n1. Import this file + `Setor.in.postman_environment.json`\n2. Top-right dropdown → **Setor.in Local Dev**\n3. Backend & docker running (`make up` + `go run ./cmd/api`)\n4. Just click any request → token auto-fills, then request runs\n\n## Switching user (admin / super_admin)\nEdit env vars `user_email` & `user_password`. Token will auto-refresh on next request.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{access_token}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Auto-token: ensure access_token in env is fresh before any request.",
          "// Skips for requests that DON'T need a token (e.g. health, login itself).",
          "const skipPaths = ['/health', '/realms/'];",
          "const url = pm.request.url.toString();",
          "if (skipPaths.some(p => url.includes(p))) return;",
          "",
          "// Decode current token if any; check exp claim with 30s safety buffer.",
          "function tokenIsFresh() {",
          "  const t = pm.environment.get('access_token');",
          "  if (!t) return false;",
          "  try {",
          "    const payload = JSON.parse(atob(t.split('.')[1]));",
          "    const now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);",
          "    return payload.exp - now > 30;",
          "  } catch (e) { return false; }",
          "}",
          "",
          "if (tokenIsFresh()) return;",
          "",
          "// Token missing or expired — fetch a new one synchronously.",
          "const kcBase  = pm.environment.get('kc_base_url');",
          "const kcRealm = pm.environment.get('kc_realm');",
          "const cid     = pm.environment.get('kc_web_client_id');",
          "const email   = pm.environment.get('user_email');",
          "const pwd     = pm.environment.get('user_password');",
          "",
          "if (!email || !pwd) {",
          "  console.error('user_email / user_password not set in environment');",
          "  return;",
          "}",
          "",
          "console.log('[auto-token] fetching new token for', email);",
          "",
          "pm.sendRequest({",
          "  url: `${kcBase}/realms/${kcRealm}/protocol/openid-connect/token`,",
          "  method: 'POST',",
          "  header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },",
          "  body: {",
          "    mode: 'urlencoded',",
          "    urlencoded: [",
          "      { key: 'grant_type', value: 'password' },",
          "      { key: 'client_id',  value: cid },",
          "      { key: 'username',   value: email },",
          "      { key: 'password',   value: pwd },",
          "      { key: 'scope',      value: 'openid profile email' }",
          "    ]",
          "  }",
          "}, (err, res) => {",
          "  if (err) { console.error('[auto-token] error', err); return; }",
          "  if (res.code !== 200) { console.error('[auto-token] status', res.code, res.text()); return; }",
          "  const j = res.json();",
          "  pm.environment.set('access_token', j.access_token);",
          "  pm.environment.set('refresh_token', j.refresh_token);",
          "  try {",
          "    const payload = JSON.parse(atob(j.access_token.split('.')[1]));",
          "    pm.environment.set('keycloak_id', payload.sub);",
          "    console.log('[auto-token] OK as', payload.email, '| roles:', payload.realm_access.roles.join(', '));",
          "  } catch (e) {}",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 — Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base_url}}/health",
              "host": ["{{api_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('db is ok', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.checks.db).to.eql('ok');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "01 — Auth (Keycloak) [optional]",
      "description": "Manual login/refresh. Usually NOT needed because auto-token at collection level handles it.\n\nUse this folder only if you want to inspect raw Keycloak response or force a fresh token.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Manual Login (force refresh token)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "password" },
                { "key": "client_id",  "value": "{{kc_web_client_id}}" },
                { "key": "username",   "value": "{{user_email}}" },
                { "key": "password",   "value": "{{user_password}}" },
                { "key": "scope",      "value": "openid profile email" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{kc_base_url}}/realms/{{kc_realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token",
              "host": ["{{kc_base_url}}"],
              "path": ["realms", "{{kc_realm}}", "protocol", "openid-connect", "token"]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('login ok', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.environment.set('access_token', j.access_token);",
                  "pm.environment.set('refresh_token', j.refresh_token);",
                  "try {",
                  "  const payload = JSON.parse(atob(j.access_token.split('.')[1]));",
                  "  pm.environment.set('keycloak_id', payload.sub);",
                  "  console.log('Logged in as', payload.email);",
                  "  console.log('Roles:', payload.realm_access.roles.join(', '));",
                  "} catch (e) {}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
